    skos:closeMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q35101402> ;
    skos:definition "the yellowish wood of tho olive-tree which takes a good polish and, being beautifully feathered, is worked up into small ornamental fancy articles: in France and other parts of the Continent, it is used as a building wood. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 277]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_olive_wood" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Olive Wood"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0070 (Wood Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 277."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
